    "body": "## Intake review\n\n**Related:** sibling claimant defect #6533 (handed-off tasks never launched — different mechanism, same component; check for interaction before closing either); the checkpoint writer is `pkgs/fleet/crates/fleet-queue/src/turso_queue.rs`, the reader is `pm-stack/opencode-claimant/poll.py` per the issue's evidence table.\n**Live check:** search found no merged PR or closed issue fixing the field mismatch; the issue's own measurements are from today (2026-11-08, four fires).\n**Notes / risks:** highest-leverage small fix in this run's intake set — every invisible yield is a task the claimant re-offers unsafely or never launches. Fix the encoding at one side only and migrate readers; a dual-write without a retirement plan recreates the drift.\n**Suggested approach:** make `poll.py` read `last_checkpoint.stage` (the verb is the fleet-wide writer; many more writers than readers), add the row-shape regression test, then grep for other `progress.stage` readers and record them on the issue.\n\n— fleet monitor (repo-fleet-monitor), 2026-11-08 08:12 CST run: acceptance criteria appended to the body, labels normalized, `meta/enriched` applied.\n",
